---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
import Container from '@components/container.astro'
import Breadcrumbs from '@components/ui/breadcrumbs.astro'
import { SITE, PLAN } from '@config/site'

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Terms', path: '/terms' }]
const updated = 'August 2026'
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Service"
	description="The terms that apply to using Astro-Menu, covering subscriptions, billing, cancellation, acceptable use and the content you upload."
	breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
	<Container class="md:max-w-screen-md">
		<Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

		<article class="py-14">
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-ink md:text-5xl">Terms of Service</h1>
			<p class="mt-3 text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

			<div
				class="prose dark:prose-invert prose-lg mt-10 max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-a:text-brandInk prose-strong:text-ink"
			>
				<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
				<p>
					These terms govern your use of {SITE.name}, a hosted digital menu service. Contacting us
					about anything in this document is easiest at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>
						{SITE.email}
					</a>.
				</p>

				<h2>2. What the service does</h2>
				<p>
					{SITE.name} hosts your menu as a web page and gives you a QR code and link that point at
					it. The service does not take orders, process payments, or act as an intermediary in any
					transaction between you and your customers.
				</p>

				<h2>3. Your account</h2>
				<p>
					You are responsible for keeping your login details secure and for everything done through
					your account. Tell us promptly if you believe someone else has gained access to it.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Subscriptions and billing</h2>
				<p>
					The service is charged per venue at {PLAN.monthly.aed} AED per month, or {PLAN.annual.aed}
					AED per year. A venue means one location with its own menu and QR code. Monthly subscriptions
					renew each month until cancelled; annual subscriptions renew each year.
				</p>
				<p>
					Prices shown in US dollars are indicative conversions provided for convenience. Billing is
					in AED unless we have agreed otherwise with you in writing.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Free trial</h2>
				<p>
					New accounts include a {PLAN.trialDays}-day trial that does not require payment details. If
					you do not subscribe by the end of the trial, the account simply stops.
				</p>

				<h2>6. Cancelling</h2>
				<p>
					You can cancel at any time. Monthly subscriptions end at the close of the current billing
					period, and annual subscriptions at the end of the paid year. When a subscription ends,
					your menu stops being served and your QR codes stop resolving — please bear that in mind if
					your codes are printed on packaging.
				</p>

				<h2>7. Your content</h2>
				<p>
					Your menu content — item names, descriptions, prices, photos and branding — remains yours.
					You grant us only the permission needed to host, display and back up that content in order
					to run the service. You are responsible for having the right to use anything you upload,
					including photographs.
				</p>

				<h2>8. Accuracy of your menu</h2>
				<p>
					You are responsible for the accuracy of your menu, including prices and any allergen or
					dietary information. We provide tools to label items; we cannot verify what is in your
					food, and the labels you apply are your representations to your customers, not ours.
				</p>

				<h2>9. Acceptable use</h2>
				<p>
					Do not use the service to publish unlawful content, to impersonate another business, or to
					attempt to disrupt the service for other customers. Menu views are unlimited under a fair
					usage policy; if traffic to a single venue is so far outside normal restaurant patterns
					that it affects other customers, we will contact you before taking any action.
				</p>

				<h2>10. Availability</h2>
				<p>
					We work to keep the service available continuously but do not guarantee uninterrupted
					operation. Planned maintenance will be scheduled outside peak dining hours where possible.
				</p>

				<h2>11. Liability</h2>
				<p>
					To the extent permitted by law, our total liability arising from the service is limited to
					the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim. We are not liable for lost
					profits or indirect losses.
				</p>

				<h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
				<p>
					We may update these terms. If a change materially affects you, we will give notice by
					email before it takes effect.
				</p>

				<h2>13. Governing law</h2>
				<p>
					These terms are governed by the laws of the United Arab Emirates, and the courts of the
					UAE have jurisdiction over any dispute.
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</Container>
</Layout>
